{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed embed is rebuilt from the browser source that carries the standing guard.\n\nExact clean pushed head b1daa56710e5c8df3d2c7d9035682cb9e99f30be on request/signing-standing-repair; tree b6d2c14a4f38890fe08caaf8555cab30273f8a4a, checkout clean, origin matching by commit SHA. Supersedes my candidate ea14bf36 at this path.\n\nWHY THIS IS ITS OWN ARTIFACT AND NOT A FOOTNOTE. Editing ui/ without running make ui leaves gs serve on the previous bundle, so the fix is in the tree, passes every Go gate, and is absent from the surface anyone actually uses. ui-check is not in the Go gates, which means nothing in `go test ./...` catches it. The embed is therefore rebuilt in the same head as the source change rather than in a follow-up commit, and recorded here so the succession is visible at this path rather than inferred from the ui artifact.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. `make ui` rebuilt the bundle; internal/service/uidist/index.html now names assets/index-BaUnpBG-.js, replacing index-DWUFVY02.js. That is the only difference at this path, and it is a build product of the source recorded in the ui artifact at this same head. Nothing here was hand-edited.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt clean, go build, go vet, go test ./... and internal/docset with -count=1 all pass; ui tsc clean; 115 ui tests pass.","body":{"commit":"b1daa56710e5c8df3d2c7d9035682cb9e99f30be","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}